  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Arthik Anusnadhan Kendra (AAK)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The rising inequality has created disparity in accessing public health and education services in society. The main reason for the rise in inequality is unequal opportunities and access to basic public services. The most sufferers in society on this front are marginalized Scheduled Caste (SC or Dalit), Scheduled Tribe (ST), and girls facing multiple forms of exclusion in society. Through the findings of various research and studies, it became evident that to meet the expenses of education and health services, marginalized sections are pushed down to poverty. There has been an increasing trend of privatization of health and education services, which has further led to the exclusion of marginalized sections. The role of private service providers in both education and healthcare services is crucial, but at the same time, there should be a proper regulatory mechanism to safeguard the rights of patients&apos; and parents&apos; (or children), especially those from marginalized (SC, ST, women, and girls, Economically Weaker Section) sections. The project &apos;Discrimination -Free Access to Education and Health Services&apos; strives to strengthen public healthcare and education services, while on the other hand, efforts are made to regulate private healthcare and education service providers. The project will strengthen the public healthcare and education systems by raising issues of discrimination and quality services at the grassroots and addressing gaps in policy or its implementation through volunteers and like -minded people working on the issue. The project will develop the capacity of the community, including parents, mothers&apos; groups, and citizens, to identify gaps in implementation and issues of discrimination, support them in doing community -based monitoring of services, and help them raise grievances through appropriate grievance redressal mechanisms. The development of the decentralized plan by engaging panchayats and local authorities is one of the focus areas. The project creates an</narrative>
  </description>
